        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright (c) 2006 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Coronary artery compression is a rare and potentially fatal complication after pulmonary valve replacement. This report describes myocardial infarction from extrinsic left main coronary artery compression after pulmonary valve replacement in a 10-y-old boy. He was successfully treated with percutaneous coronary intervention."
